em  because it's just wasting their time  now when people start flicking through  your portfolio the first thing they're  always impressed with  is render quality render quality in the  industry doesn't mean  abstract photoshop artistic imagery it  means genuine knowledge of architectural  rendering software  so if you're a gun at 3ds max or if you  know exactly how to use v-ray to create  incredible imagery showcase that you  don't want to be going and showing  generic photoshop things slap together  you  genuinely want to show as much knowledge  as you can  because your portfolio is showcasing  your skills and your abilities  the render quality only goes so far  though because if these ideas are  generic  nobody's going gonna care if you just  showcase a little baby house  in the back of some suburban village  it's gonna look nice but nobody's gonna  go wow this guy's got  incredible ideas or wow this girl knows  exactly what she's talking about  they really want to be wowed and they  want to be impressed  so whatever your abstract idea is make  sure it's grand  but make sure it is buildable from  somebody who's interviewed a number of  grads  make sure those ideas are buildable it  is the first thing i pick on grads  and it's their knowledge of  documentation nobody expects your  knowledge to be perfect but make sure  you've done some research and some  understanding of why things come  together  and how they come together so if you do  have a grand abstract master idea  be sure you know what it's being built  out of how it's going to be built  is it constructable is it feasible could  it  actually be built if it could be built  and you've documented it in such a way  that somebody could take some plans and  build it  that is incredible and something  everybody looks forward to  it doesn't matter if you're doing a  thesis or a job interview  knowing how something is constructed is  pivotal  now if you're applying for a new job and  you've already been in the profession  for a little while  you want to focus on the projects that  are completed there probably isn't too  many but a completed project  is much more valuable than one that's  theoretically still on the drawing board  anybody can go and design something  theoretically but not many people can  take the project from start to finish  if you can showcase real images real  photography and videography  of a finished project as well as the  construction documentation  of that project it's going to be  incredibly useful  because somebody who's employing you is  going to be able to go hmm  this person has documented this seen it  through to construction  gone out there visited the project kept  the connection with the client  and potentially brought in more work  later on the next key criteria  is time management and performance data  if your old work has this information on  you make sure you keep it  because understanding your performance  understanding your time management  is pivotal in your next position by  showcasing to your employer that they're  going to pay you x  but you can generate y that's 160 times  better than x  nobody wants somebody that is going to  come into the job and cost them 10 times  more than they're paying them  everybody has overheads everybody costs  a certain figure to sit in that seat  so as a new employee you want to make  sure you're generating  more money than you cost if you have  this information  it's vital i know it seems a little bit  random but  it's something that every employer and  every business owner is going to be  looking at  critically and going this guy knows  exactly what's going on now in both  situations you want to showcase at least  one page about you  it needs to be about your hobbies your  goals your aspirations  the knowledge you have behind you what  programs you know what skills you have  saying in a portfolio that you're a good  photographer  might mean to the employer that you have  a new social media content creator  or that you've been in e-commerce before  all of a sudden you know somebody that  is good at marketing  there are so many different things that  we do outside of our professional life  and in our own personal lives  that can be brought on board to be able  to better our position  so make sure you really talk about who  you are  as a person because it's just as  critical as who you are and how you  perform in that role  now because you've spent so much time  putting this portfolio together  you want to make sure the actual  portfolio is of quality  so the presentation of it needs to be  perfect one  think about a box some sort of  presentation method of how you can hand  over  this special book to the person who's  either getting the thesis  employing you in the future or that you  just want them to see  you don't want to be just handing over a  usb and going this is my work  look at it flick through the pages you  might be excited you want to genuinely  excite them with an  unboxing experience inside that box the  paper quality obviously has to be  perfect it has to be thick card  it has to be printed well if something  hasn't printed correctly go back and  print it again you don't want to be in  an interview and going oh that didn't  print right  because it shows you didn't pay enough  attention to the details  you didn't care enough to go and reprint  that that's why in university they told  you  never go to your drawing board and  scribble in your name or your student  number if you've forgotten it  because it means you didn't think about  the details everybody's going to spot  that pencil mark  but they might not necessarily spot the  mistake now if you really want to stand  out from the crowd  forget about paper completely scrap that  entire idea and forget  everything i just said i know  controversial right right now in 2021  more and more architecture is being  presented in a video format  every single day we're creating video  content just like this video that you're  watching now  to showcase to people around the world  so if somebody was to present their  thesis  or their job application to me via a  well-constructed 3d animated movie with  some  amazing footage of constructed projects  that if they're applying for a new job  for  i'd be so impressed i'd know that this  person has gone  so far above and beyond to make sure  they stand out from the crowd  everybody in the architecture industry  is good at compiling documentation  not many people are good at presenting  videos  so if you can take it a step up take it  to the next level  don't forget about the unboxing  experience and create something  incredible  this is definitely going to make sure  you stand out from the crowd anyway  that's all for me today guys thank you  so much for watching  i hope this video gives you some  inspiration and good guidance of how you  can create your next architectural  portfolio  if it did make sure you smash that  subscribe button below because this  video forms one of my 28 videos  in 28 days usually it would be i'll see  you next monday  but in this case i'll see you tomorrow
 

